usage: run.py [-h] --kernel KERNEL --kernel-release KERNEL_RELEASE
              --module-root MODULE_ROOT --cache CACHE --pin PIN
              --recipe RECIPE [--reference REFERENCE]
              [--firmware-pmi FIRMWARE_PMI] [--firmware-dtb FIRMWARE_DTB]
              [--external-network-fixture] [--network-fixture]
              [--command-probe] [--without-label-policy]
              [--label-fault-second-filesystem]
              output

Build a real distro in a disposable VM; no privileged host operations.

positional arguments:
  output

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --kernel KERNEL
  --kernel-release KERNEL_RELEASE
  --module-root MODULE_ROOT
  --cache CACHE
  --pin PIN
  --recipe RECIPE
  --reference REFERENCE
  --firmware-pmi FIRMWARE_PMI
  --firmware-dtb FIRMWARE_DTB
  --external-network-fixture
                        Serve a loopback-only host TCP endpoint reached
                        through VM outbound networking
  --network-fixture     Serve controlled guest DNS/TCP and assert network
                        cleanup
  --command-probe       Commit safe syscall probe and keyctl runtime into
                        fixture context
  --without-label-policy
                        Negative validation only: omit environment policy
                        loading
  --label-fault-second-filesystem
                        VM-only differential test: reject the second
                        filesystem label probe
